1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,857
This crypto site posted returns of about one percent a day. Sounds small. It's the dumbest number in crypto.

2
00:00:06,757 --> 00:00:12,046
BitConnect. Twenty seventeen. You hand over Bitcoin, a so-called trading bot does its thing, you get paid.

3
00:00:12,296 --> 00:00:15,635
So let's just do the math. A thousand bucks, at one percent a day.

4
00:00:15,885 --> 00:00:18,019
After one year? Thirty-seven thousand.

5
00:00:18,819 --> 00:00:20,596
Year two? One point four million.

6
00:00:20,796 --> 00:00:23,786
Year three? Fifty-four— okay, fifty-three point nine million.

7
00:00:24,086 --> 00:00:27,228
By day thirteen eighty-nine, you're a billionaire. Off one grand.

8
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:29,526
No bot does that. Nothing does that.

9
00:00:30,426 --> 00:00:37,259
So where'd the money come from? Prosecutors say newer investors' money paid the older ones. About two point four billion dollars came in.

10
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:40,800
January twenty eighteen, it shut down. And the coin collapsed.

11
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:45,675
Its top US promoter pleaded guilty. Thirty-eight months.

12
00:00:46,575 --> 00:00:50,410
So if a bot really made one percent a day, why would it need your money? Comment.

13
00:00:50,974 --> 00:00:52,447
Follow for the next one.
